  "description": "The Best Strategy...and then not. What to do....",
  "body_html": "<p>Happy Tuesday! </p><p>If you have a stock you want me to review, leave it here on the<em><strong> <a href=\"https://substack.com/@stocktok/note/c-317238380?r=4z8lgl&amp;utm_source=notes-share-action&amp;utm_medium=web\">Mid-Week Movers Requests Note (Click here)</a>. </strong></em>This series that we do, usually weekly, depending on market conditions, has produced consistent top stocks to buy. </p><p>Market is pretty quiet today. After hitting an all time high last week, it has since been taking a breath. I know these days are not exciting, but they are normal. We are not seeing any collapses, or breaks in structure. Just standard pull backs, for the time being. </p><p>On days like this, I usually focus on something educational or news related. Today, I wanted to share some insights to Technical Analysis… also known as “Bro Astrology”. I think its great to learn. Understanding the differences between a exponential moving average and a simple moving average, can only help you. Evaluating if a stock is overbought or oversold, can only help you. </p><p>If you want to talk about any specific indicator, feel free to ask me in the <em><strong><a href=\"https://open.substack.com/chat/posts/8aac3321-fed7-4dd4-a536-a9fb92d3e2bb\">Main Chat</a></strong></em>. Not to sound egotistical… but I know all of them, or darn close. Including the math and strategies behind them. I’m an analytical nerd that has been studying the market for 19 years now. My capstone thesis at the U.S. Naval Academy was “Predicting Stock Market Movements with Multi-Variable Regression Analysis.” Trust me. </p><p>But you never hear me talk about indicators really. Why? Because I don’t really use them. I use NAKED charts. And they all work…until they don’t. I saw so many people lose money, forcing strategies that worked in 2021, but not in 2022. Losing all the euphoric gains they made. </p><p>We sat out of the market from January 2025 to June 2025. Why? The strategy was not working. Regardless whether you are a short term trader or a multi-year investor, you have to respect price action. An oversold RSI does not automatically mean that the stock price will go up. </p><p>Anyways, check out the video, I give examples and more explanation there. </p><p>The few indicators that I did build, can be found in the <em><strong><a href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/the-stocktok-playbook-everything?r=4z8lgl\">StockTok Playbook</a></strong></em>. Help yourself, they are free and you can apply them to TradingView. They are predominantly price action based, and many people have been using them for several years now. </p><p>Again, quiet day. Not much to say right now. But there is always calm before the storm (good or bad). So don’t run away. I will keep you updated as we progress. I am expecting more all time highs in the near future. </p><p>Be sure to like and re-stack!</p><p>Thanks for stopping by!</p><p>Timothy (aka StockTok) </p><div class=\"community-chat\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://open.substack.com/pub/tjstocks/chat?utm_source=chat_embed&quot;,&quot;subdomain&quot;:&quot;tjstocks&quot;,&quot;pub&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:3537822,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Timothy’s StockTok&quot;,&quot;author_name&quot;:&quot;StockTok 📈&quot;,&quot;author_photo_url&quot;:&quot;https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!W3S9!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F8add7fc9-8edc-4748-ba33-360428e75ee1_1206x1206.png&quot;}}\" data-component-name=\"CommunityChatRenderPlaceholder\"></div>",
